---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const decisions = [
	{
		title: 'A static site, not server rendering',
		text: 'Pages are built ahead of time and served as plain files, so production has no Node process.',
		pro: 'Fast pages and very little memory. The site stays up even if the API goes down.',
		con: 'Any content change needs a new build and deployment.',
	},
	{
		title: 'SQLite, not Postgres',
		text: 'The only data is contact messages, stored in a database file used by this site alone.',
		pro: 'No database server competing for 2 GB of RAM.',
		con: 'One writer at a time and a single machine. Backups need care, because copying a live file is not safe.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Cloudflare Tunnel, not open ports',
		text: 'A connector inside the laptop opens the connection outward, and Cloudflare handles HTTPS.',
		pro: 'No open ports on my home network and no need for a public IP.',
		con: 'The site depends on Cloudflare, which also sits in the path of all its traffic.',
	},
	{
		title: 'Build in CI, never on the server',
		text: 'GitHub Actions runs the checks and builds the images. The laptop only downloads and runs them.',
		pro: 'A slow laptop never compiles anything, and what runs is what was tested.',
		con: 'Deployments depend on GitHub Actions and its image registry.',
	},
	{
		title: 'One laptop, one point of failure',
		text: 'If the power or the internet goes out at home, the site goes with it. There is no second server.',
		pro: 'It stays simple, and an external monitor can detect outages from outside the house.',
		con: 'Downtime is real. The mitigation is noticing quickly and having a tested way to restore backups.',
	},
	{
		title: 'What it costs',
		text: 'A domain, and nothing else.',
		pro: 'The hardware already existed and the services used have free tiers.',
		con: 'I am the operations team, so every failure is mine to fix.',
	},
];
---

<Layout
	title="About this site"
	description="How and why this site runs on a 2014 laptop: the architecture, the decisions and their trade-offs."
>
	<h1>This site runs on a 2014 laptop</h1>
	<p class="lead">An ASUS X200MA with a Celeron N2830, 2 GB of RAM and a 500 GB hard drive.</p>

	<p style="margin-top: 2.5rem">
		I could have put this on a free hosting platform in ten minutes. Instead, it's a working example of how I
		think about software: start from the real constraints, choose the simplest thing that fits and be honest
		about what each choice costs.
	</p>

	<h2>How a request gets here</h2>
	<ol class="flow">
		<li>Your browser connects to Cloudflare over HTTPS.</li>
		<li>Cloudflare forwards the request through a tunnel to the laptop.</li>
		<li>Caddy serves the static pages and passes <code>/api/*</code> to FastAPI.</li>
		<li>FastAPI stores contact messages in SQLite, then sends a notification.</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>The decisions</h2>
	{
		decisions.map(({ title, text, pro, con }) => (
			<section>
				<h3>{title}</h3>
				<p>{text}</p>
				<ul class="tradeoffs">
					<li>
						<strong>Pro</strong> {pro}
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Con</strong> {con}
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
		))
	}
</Layout>
